#: zypp_desk/pages/repotools.py:18
msgid ""
"Every repository has a priority, a number from 1 to 200. When a package is "
"in more than one repository, zypper takes it from the one with the lowest "
"number, even if another one has a newer version. With the same number, the "
"newest version wins, wherever it comes from.\n"
"\n"
"99 is the default. A lower number (90) makes a repository win: useful for "
"the codecs of VideoLAN or Packman. A higher number (110, 120) makes it give "
"way: useful for personal repositories, so that they only bring what openSUSE "
"does not have.\n"
"\n"
"zypper also keeps each package with the vendor it came from: a priority "
"alone does not move a program from openSUSE to another vendor (that needs "
"“Allow a change of vendor”)."
